  "body": "## Problem\n\nPR #3855 set `level_rings::SIDE_EPS` from 1 um to 10 um. The old value was below the 5 um flats of the arcs, so the planner read parts of the part wall as stock edge (#3825). The new value is a fixed number. If the arc tolerance changes, the same fault can come back.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Export the arc tolerance (the chord or flat tolerance) from `geo2d`.\n- Set `SIDE_EPS` from that value with a fixed safety factor, for example two times the flat tolerance.\n- Keep the pins of #3855, including the 0.1 mm real-wall pin.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Follow-up from the review of PR #3855.\n",
